//! The card-play pipeline: `_apply_action_impl`'s play branch and the
//! `_run_steps_inner` step dispatch.
//!
//! Python spreads one card play across a resumable `CardPlayFrame` with seven
//! stages, because a body can block on a player selection and has to be
//! resumed by a later action. Most admitted plays still finish synchronously,
//! but an admitted replay whose body selects a physical card parks one closed
//! `CardPlay` continuation. The frame is the stack/resume token and
//! `HotState.pending` owns the exact payload exposed on the canonical wire;
//! every other blocking shape remains fail-closed. Resumption runs only the
//! selected replay body, then returns to the ordinary finish/fanout/routing
//! order without paying the outer play's resources a second time.
//!
//! Stage order, from `_apply_action_impl` (frozen Python, deleted #2827) and
//! `_advance_card_play_frame`:
//!
//! 1. `CanPlay` gates, then remove the exact instance from Hand;
//! 2. `SpendResources`: energy first (`AfterEnergySpent`), then Stars;
//! 3. `OnPlayWrapper` places every played instance in Play, including
//!    direct AutoPlay sources; it resolves
//!    result location **before** play-count generation;
//! 4. `GeneratePlayCount` (the exact Burst, One-Two Punch, Echo Form and
//!    Signal Boost listeners are synchronous here; the remaining replay
//!    sources stay refused);
//! 5. `CardPlayStarted` history, then the started-play counters;
//! 6. the body — the step program;
//! 7. `CardPlayFinished` history, then `_finish_card_play`'s result routing.

use crate::catalog::{
    CardIdentity, CardSpec, CardTargetType, Catalog, CompiledArg, ForgeRehearsal,
};
